Package: tmeld
Architecture: all
Depends: python3 (>= 3.10)
Recommends: git,
            python3-aiohttp (>= 3.9),
Suggests: meld
Description: Meld, in your terminal - TUI diff and merge tool
 A faithful terminal port of GNOME Meld: the same diff engine (vendored
 verbatim from Meld), the same colors, the same keybindings - usable
 over plain SSH.
 .
 Features two- and three-way file comparison and merging with the git
 mergetool contract, folder comparison, a version-control status view,
 and anti-aliased linkmap graphics on sixel or kitty-graphics capable
 terminals.
 .
 Also ships bmeld, the same program served to a browser (tmeld --web).
 That needs python3-aiohttp, which Debian provides and which is therefore
 a Recommends rather than a bundled copy: aiohttp carries C extensions,
 and vendoring it would make this an architecture-dependent package.
 .
 This package bundles its Python dependencies (Textual and friends)
 under /usr/share/tmeld because tmeld requires newer versions than
 Debian ships; it does not interfere with system Python packages.
